# The two-letter band comparison map from a group action on a tree

This file records the **Bass--Serre reduction** of the target
`Work.OROneRel.twoLetterBandComparison_injective` (the injectivity of
`hnnConjMap (winVertex …) (mk (tlLowTau p q))`, i.e. Linton's `π₁`-computation for the ladder of
band domains): the target follows from the existence of an action of
`G = ⟨a, b | (tlU p q) ^ l⟩` on a tree **without inversions** with a vertex `v` whose stabiliser is
exactly the band vertex `winVertex Wt (tlW p q) 0 (p*q) (tlU p q) l`, together with an edge `v ⟶ z`
satisfying `mk (tlLowTau p q) • z = v`.

That is `Work.OROneRel.hnnConjMap_injective_of_tree` (`hnnConjMap_injective_of_tree.lean`) with the
vertex stabiliser rewritten by `hstab`; no further input is needed.

## How the tree is produced (see `Submission/Work/OROneRel/NOTES_twoLetterBandComparison_injective.md`)

* `H₀ := (winRho Wt c 0 (p*q)).range ≤ F₂ = FreeGroup (Fin 2)` is the fundamental group of the band
  graph; the telescoping identity `winRho_winRoot` gives `tlU p q ∈ H₀`;
* `winVertex … = H₀.map (PresentedGroup.mk _)`;
* by the one-dimensional case of Linton's `splitting` (*One-relator hierarchies*, arXiv 2202.11324,
  §3; the band graph of the two-petal rose is a `Z`-domain of its `Z`-cover) there is an `F₂`-tree
  `V` without inversions whose vertex `v` has stabiliser exactly `H₀`, together with an edge
  `v ⟶ z` with `tlLowTau p q • z = v`; this is the statement `Work.OROneRel.winRhoRange_tree`
  (`Submission/Work/OROneRel/winRhoRange_tree.lean`, **proved**);
* the normal closure `N = Subgroup.normalClosure {tlU p q ^ l}` is generated by the elliptic element
  `tlU p q ^ l` (which fixes `v` because `tlU p q ∈ H₀ = Stab v`), so by
  `Work.ORBassSerre.Action.isTree_orbitV_of_normalClosure_elliptic` the quotient graph `V ⧸ N` is a
  tree, and `G = F₂ ⧸ N = PresentedGroup {tlU p q ^ l}` acts on it with
  `MulAction.stabilizer G [v] = H₀.map (PresentedGroup.mk _) = winVertex …`; the edge `[v] ⟶ [z]`
  still satisfies `mk τ • [z] = [v]`.  The two inputs of this step,
  `isTree_orbitV_of_normalClosure_elliptic` and `quotient_actsWithoutInversions`
  (`Work.ORDunwoody.freeOnTreeIsFree_quotient`), are both already proved in the workspace; only the
  Lean plumbing of the universes remains (see §14.5 of the notes).

## A failed design, recorded

An earlier draft packaged the tree data in a `class FreeBandTree`/`FreeBandTree₀` with the
`Quiver`/`GraphAction`/… instances as *instance fields*, in order to make them available to instance
search.  That design does not work: the class's data field `V : Type` is not determined by the class
parameters, so instance search cannot use the instance fields (the failure is
`failed to synthesize instance of type class Quiver FreeBandTree₀.V`).  See §14.5 of the notes for
the working recipe.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.twoLetterTlDefs
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.twoLetter_generation
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.winAssembly
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.hnnConjSplit
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.hnnConjMap_injective_of_tree

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Work.OROneRel

/-- **The target from a `G`-action on a tree.**  A `G`-tree without inversions, a vertex `v` whose
stabiliser is the band vertex `winVertex …`, and an edge `v ⟶ z` closed up by the image of
`tlLowTau p q` force the canonical comparison map of the pair `(winVertex …, mk (tlLowTau p q))` to
be injective. -/
theorem hnnConjMap_injective_of_treeData (p q l : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) (hq : 1 ≤ q) (hl : 1 ≤ l)
    (hcop : Nat.Coprime p q) (Wt : ℤ → FreeGroup (Fin 2)) (hW0 : Wt 0 = 1)
    (hcoh : ∀ i : ℤ, Work.OROneRel.cohom (Work.OROneRel.tlW p q) (Wt i) = Multiplicative.ofAdd i)
    (hwin : ∀ e ∈ Work.OROneRel.decor (Work.OROneRel.tlW p q) 0
        (Work.OROneRel.wordOf (Work.OROneRel.tlU p q)),
      Work.OROneRel.coverEdge e ∈ Work.OROneRel.winE (Work.OROneRel.tlW p q) 0
        ((p : ℤ) * (q : ℤ)))
    {V : Type} [Quiver V] [Quiver.HasInvolutiveReverse V]
    [MulAction (PresentedGroup ({Work.OROneRel.tlU p q ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup (Fin 2)))) V]
    [Work.ORBassSerre.GraphAction
      (PresentedGroup ({Work.OROneRel.tlU p q ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup (Fin 2)))) V]
    (hT : Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree V)
    (hninv : Work.ORBassSerre.ActsWithoutInversions
      (PresentedGroup ({Work.OROneRel.tlU p q ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup (Fin 2)))) V)
    (v : V) {z : V} (e : v ⟶ z)
    (hstab : MulAction.stabilizer
        (PresentedGroup ({Work.OROneRel.tlU p q ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup (Fin 2)))) v =
      Work.OROneRel.winVertex Wt (Work.OROneRel.tlW p q) 0 ((p : ℤ) * (q : ℤ))
        (Work.OROneRel.tlU p q) l)
    (hclose : (PresentedGroup.mk ({Work.OROneRel.tlU p q ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup (Fin 2)))
        (Work.OROneRel.tlLowTau p q hp hq hcop)) • z = v) :
    Function.Injective (Work.OROneRel.hnnConjMap
      (Work.OROneRel.winVertex Wt (Work.OROneRel.tlW p q) 0 ((p : ℤ) * (q : ℤ))
        (Work.OROneRel.tlU p q) l)
      (PresentedGroup.mk ({Work.OROneRel.tlU p q ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup (Fin 2)))
        (Work.OROneRel.tlLowTau p q hp hq hcop))) := by
  have hkey := hnnConjMap_injective_of_tree (G :=
      PresentedGroup ({Work.OROneRel.tlU p q ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup (Fin 2)))) hT hninv v
    (PresentedGroup.mk ({Work.OROneRel.tlU p q ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup (Fin 2)))
      (Work.OROneRel.tlLowTau p q hp hq hcop)) e hclose
  rwa [hstab] at hkey

end Work.OROneRel
